[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Replay.replay","page":"API","text":"replay(instructions::Vector{<:AbstractString}, buf::IO; kwargs...)\n\nReplay the REPL output from given instructions.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nReplay options\n\nuse_ghostwriter: Flag to enable ghostwriter mode. (default: false)\nstartup_prompt: Text to wait for when the child REPL starts. (default: \"julia>\")\nprompt_delimiter: Text ending each subsequent prompt. (default: \"> \") For numbered prompts use startup_prompt=\"In [1]: \", prompt_delimiter=\"]: \", and leave use_ghostwriter=false; ghostwriter assumes the standard prompts.\n\nJulia options\n\njulia_project: Path to a project where julia process runs. (default: @.)\ncmd: Additional command for julia process. (default: \"--color=yes\")\n\nNumbered prompts\n\nInitialize Julia's REPL interface before enabling numbered prompts:\n\nreplay([\"1 + 1\", \"ans * 2\"];\n    cmd=`-q --color=no -e 'using REPL; atreplinit(repl -> (repl.interface = REPL.setup_interface(repl); REPL.numbered_prompt!(repl)))'`,\n    startup_prompt=\"In [1]: \", prompt_delimiter=\"]: \")\n\nInteractive menus\n\nASCII REPL.TerminalMenus menus can be replayed with the default prompt delimiter. Put the request and its response in separate instructions and use a carriage return (\"\\r\") to confirm a selection:\n\nreplay([\n    \"using REPL.TerminalMenus\",\n    \"menu = RadioMenu([\"apple\", \"orange\"]);\",\n    \"choice = request(\"Choose fruit:\", menu)\",\n    \"$(DOWN_ARROW)\\r\",\n    \"@show choice\",\n])\n\nUse \"q\" to cancel a TerminalMenus request. Menu requests must display the configured prompt_delimiter; arbitrary full-screen TUIs or menus with different cursor styles are not automatically detected. Keep use_ghostwriter=false for raw menu keystrokes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Replay.replay"},{"category":"macro","location":"api/#Replay.@deparse-Tuple{Any}","page":"API","text":"@deparse expr\n\nCreate a string from expr. It tries to output something similar to we type in Julia REPL. If expr contains @comment <message>, it is transformed into # <message>.\n\nExamples\n\njulia> @deparse 1+1\n\"1 + 1\"\n\njulia> @deparse sin(1f0+a)\n\"sin(1.0f0 + a)\"\n\njulia> @deparse f(x) = sin(x)/x  # Sometimes not work as expected\n\"f(x) = begin\\n        sin(x) / x\\n    end\\n\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Replay.@deparse"},{"category":"section","location":"#Replay.jl","page":"Getting started","text":"Replay Julia REPL instructions automatically, including help, package and shell modes. The test suite supports the latest stable Julia (1) and the current long-term support release (lts) on Linux, macOS and Windows. Julia 1.6 is no longer supported.","title":"Replay.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Minimal-example","page":"Getting started","text":"Install Replay with import Pkg; Pkg.add(\"Replay\"), then save this as demo.jl:\n\nusing Replay\n\nreplay([\"x = 1 + 1\", \"println(\\\"Hello from Replay!\\\")\", \"@show x\"];\n       cmd=`-q --color=no`)\n\nRun it with julia --project demo.jl. Replay launches a child Julia REPL; it does not evaluate the instructions in your current session. For package-specific demos, pass julia_project explicitly to replay.\n\nTo capture text instead of displaying it:\n\noutput = replay(\"1 + 1\", IOBuffer(); cmd=`-q --color=no`)\ntext = String(take!(output))\n\nSee the API reference for options, control keys and @deparse.","title":"Minimal example"},{"category":"section","location":"#Recording","page":"Getting started","text":"Replay produces terminal output, not an MP4 file. An external terminal recorder can capture the minimal example without screen recording:\n\nasciinema rec demo.cast --command \"julia --project demo.jl\"\nasciinema play demo.cast\n\nThe full gallery, integration examples and recording/export instructions are maintained separately in ReplayGallery.jl. This manual does not execute or download those examples during its build.","title":"Recording"}]
